arna-period"><span class="enc-name">Amarna Period</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">The Amarna Period is the late Eighteenth Dynasty of Egypt in the mid-fourteenth century BCE, named after Amarna (Akhetaten), the new capital built by the pharaoh…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amarsinhji-of-wankaner"><span class="enc-name">Amarsinhji of Wankaner</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amarsinhji was the ruler, with the title Raj Sahib, of Wankaner, a princely state of the Jhala Rajputs in Kathiawar, western India, from 1881 to 1948.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amartya-sen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amartya-sen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amartya Sen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amartya Sen is an Indian economist and philosopher, born in 1933 in Santiniketan, Bengal, British India, and named by Rabindranath Tagore.</span></a></li></ul>
